; THE ONE PLACE THIS MODULE'S EXPORTS ARE DECLARED.
;
; Nothing here carries __declspec(dllexport) -- deliberately. Excel looks these
; up by their PLAIN names, and while an extern "C" __stdcall function is
; undecorated on x64, on x86 it decorates to _xlAutoOpen@0: an add-in that
; loads perfectly and exports nothing Excel can find. A .def names them
; undecorated on both targets, so this file is what keeps a future 32-bit
; build working (x64 is the supported target).
;
; ONE SOURCE, SO A MISS IS LOUD. A function missing from this list is not
; exported at all; the registration in src/app/commands.cpp then logs it as
; FAILED, rather than a second declaration silently covering for it.

EXPORTS
    xlAutoOpen
    xlAutoClose
    xlAutoFree12
    xlAddInManagerInfo12

; ARM AND DISARM, REACHABLE WITHOUT COM.
;
; These are XLL commands registered with Excel at load, so they are callable as
;   Application.Run("XRayXL_Arm")
; from VBA or from any automation client -- with no window, no focus, and no
; COM object of ours in the process.
;
; No COM class factory is exported: serving a COM add-in from this DLL would give
; it a second lifetime owner. See src/app/commands.cpp.
    XRayXL_Arm
    XRayXL_Disarm
    XRayXL_SetTraceParam
    XRayXL_GetTraceParam
    XRayXL_GetTraceSummary
    XRayXL_IsArmed
    XRayXL_FaultProbe

; WHAT GETS TRACED. Registered as FUNCTIONS rather than commands,
; because each takes arguments and returns an answer -- a command has neither
; channel:
;   Application.Run("XRayXL_SetTraceParam", "XLL", "DEPTH", "ALL")
;   Application.Run("XRayXL_GetTraceParam", "VBA", "DEPTH")
;   Application.Run("XRayXL_GetTraceSummary")
; Source is XLL or VBA, or omitted for both; Name is DEPTH (OFF/TOP/ALL), ARGS,
; RETVAL or CALLER. The setter refuses while armed and refuses when the caller
; is a cell.
;
; XRayXL_XLLTrace and XRayXL_VBATrace were removed here: they wrote the
; same state but could not express DEPTH=TOP, so setting them silently turned
; TOP into ALL. See src/app/commands.cpp.
;
